# Default mode (NFSU2_PAD=1), no controller at start (NFSU2_PAD_FAKE=PLUG=0):
# no game pad device, the game's rescan stays on.  Keyboard to a Quick Race;
# the controller plugged in mid-race is found by the rescan and drives
# (throttle on the right trigger); unplugged, the device stays and reads at
# rest (no input stuck, no DIERR_INPUTLOST); plugged back in, it drives again.
# With NFSU2_PAD=hotplug the same run shows DIERR_INPUTLOST on the unplug and
# a new device after the replug.
0:until:RETURN:MC_Background.fng:120
+200:until:RETURN:UI_QRModeSelect.fng:300
+200:until:RETURN:UI_QRTrackSelect.fng:150
+200:until:RETURN:UI_QRModeOptions.fng:150
+200:until:RETURN:UI_QRCarSelect.fng:150
+200:until:RETURN:PC_Loading.fng:150
+1500:log:race: plug the controller in, right trigger and RB held, stick left
+0:pad:PLUG=1;RT=1;RB=1;LX=-1
+120:in
+0:log:unplug
+0:pad:PLUG=0
+5:in
+60:in
+0:log:plug back in, still held
+0:pad:PLUG=1
+120:in
+0:pad:OFF
+30:in
+0:log:end
